==English==

===Etymology===
[[life|Life]] + [[en- -en]], ''intensifying verbal circumfix''.<ref name="OED-etym">The '''Oxford English Dictionary''' (2007) states that '''enliven''' was formed by the simultaneous prefixing of ''[[en-]]'' and suffixing of ''[[-en]]'', which, by definition, constitutes circumfixation.</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ɛnˈlaɪvə̆n/|lang=en}}
*: Rhymes: [[Rhymes:English:-aɪvən|-aɪvə̆n]]

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{context|obsolete|transitive|lang=en}} To give [[life]] or [[spirit]] to; to [[revive]] or [[animate]].
# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To make more [[lively]], [[cheerful]] or [[interesting]].
#: ''The game was much '''enlivened''' when both teams scored within five minutes of each other.''

